      "signature": "void PrepareCompositeUnitFrame(uint * pUnit)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Prepares composite unit frame by loading and drawing all COF components.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pUnit not NULL and has required bitmasks\n2. Validate ptGfxInfo exists at pUnit[0x2e]\n3. Search GFX info list for matching mode/direction entry\n4. Get COF data pointer and calculate component byte offset\n5. First pass: Load cel frames, track max width and loaded count\n6. Second pass: Draw each component via Ordinal_10075\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (uint*): Composite unit structure pointer\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value, draws directly to screen buffer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2e (46): GFX info pointer offset in unit\n- 0x1c (28): COF header size\n- 0x0f (15): NUM_COMPONENTS - 1 max component check\n- 0x12 (18): Cel data array clear count (72 bytes)",
