      "name": "IsItemTypeEquivalent",
      "signature": "bool IsItemTypeEquivalent(uint dwItemType, uint dwTargetType)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Checks if an item type is equivalent to or inherits from a target type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return TRUE if target type is 0 (all types inherit from null)\n2. Return FALSE if item type is 0 (null type inherits from nothing)\n3. Push item type onto traversal stack\n4. Loop: pop type, check equiv1/equiv2 parent types\n5. Push non-zero parent types onto stack\n6. Return TRUE if target found, FALSE if stack exhausted\n\nParameters:\n- dwItemType: Item type code to check (from itemtypes.txt)\n- dwTargetType: Target type code to match\n\nReturns:\n- TRUE (1): Item type is or inherits from target type\n- FALSE (0): No inheritance relationship\n\nStructure Layout:\n- Offset +0x04: equiv1 (byte) - First parent type code\n- Offset +0x05: equiv2 (byte) - Second parent type code\n- Record size: 0xEC bytes per ItemTypeTxtRecord\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xEC (236): ItemTypeTxtRecord stride\n- 14 (0x0E): Maximum stack depth for type traversal",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:96c98a60bed1615029e088e113bace9e",
