      "name": "SetUnitScaledValue",
      "signature": "void SetUnitScaledValue(void * pUnit, int nValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets a scaled and clamped value in a unit structure field.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate unit pointer (assert if NULL)\n2. Read max value from unit+0xc field\n3. Scale max value by 0x100 (256)\n4. Clamp input value to non-negative (negate if negative)\n5. Take minimum of clamped value and scaled max\n6. Store result at unit+0x8 field\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (void*): Pointer to unit structure\n- nValue (int): Value to clamp and store (can be negative)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x8: Offset of value field in unit\n- 0xc: Offset of max value field in unit\n- 0x100 (256): Scaling factor for max value",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:052a101a230c3ddc22bbf8ff66201a19",
