      "name": "DrawUnicodeTextWithColors",
      "signature": "void DrawUnicodeTextWithColors(Unicode * pszText, int nXPos, int nYPos, int nColor, int nCenter, dword dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Draws Unicode text with color codes and optional centering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate display width (with optional centering adjustment)\n2. Compute string length and initial x-offset based on centering flag\n3. Initialize character data array and set Cel data table pointer\n4. For each character in string:\n   - Detect color codes (0xFF prefix): Extract color index, validate range, adjust color\n   - Detect newline (0x0A): Reset x-offset to baseline (with centering recalc)\n   - Draw regular character using processor, advance x-offset\n5. Return after processing all characters\n\nParameters:\n- wsText (Unicode*): Unicode string to draw (may contain color/newline codes)\n- nXPos (int): Starting x-coordinate\n- nYPos (int): Starting y-coordinate\n- nColor (int): Default color index for characters\n- fCenter (int): Non-zero to center text horizontally\n- dwFlags (dword): Rendering flags (purpose unknown)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xFF: Color code prefix in Unicode string\n- 0x30: ASCII '0' for color digit offset\n- 0x0C: Maximum color index (0-12)\n- 0x0A: Newline character code\n- 0x10: Negative font height multiplier denominator\n- 18: Size of character data array (auStack_48)\n- 8: Display width padding offset",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:5f738b2f52e7ad9d12b0cca5e7ca9912",
