      "name": "InitializeImageDimensions",
      "signature": "void InitializeImageDimensions(int * pImageData, int nWidth, int nHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initialize image data structure with width and height. Validates that image data has eType field set to 2, then sets width at offset +4 and height at offset +0x48.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if pImageData->eType == 2 (assertion check)\n2. On failure, trigger assertion failure with FogAssert\n3. Set pImageData[1] = nWidth (offset +4)\n4. Set pImageData[0x12] = nHeight (offset +0x48, 18*4)\n5. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- pImageData (int*): Pointer to image data structure, must have eType=2\n- nWidth (int): Image width value to set at offset +4\n- nHeight (int): Image height value to set at offset +0x48\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success (always, or triggers assertion failure)\n\nNotes:\n- Field at offset 0 contains eType (must be 2)\n- Field at offset 4 is width storage\n- Field at offset 0x48 (72 bytes) is height storage",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:052a101a230c3ddc22bbf8ff66201a19",
