      "name": "InitializeCelFrameCount",
      "signature": "int InitializeCelFrameCount(int * pCelData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes cel animation frame count from image data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify pCelData->eType == 2 (DT_CelData), assert if not\n2. Call GetCelFrameCount to get frame count from cel image at pCelData[1]\n3. Calculate requested max - 1, clamped to frameCount - 1\n4. Clamp negative values to 0\n5. Store final clamped value in pCelData[0x40] (nFrameOffset field)\n\nParameters:\n- pCelData (int*): Pointer to cel data structure (eType field at offset 0)\n- IMPLICIT [ESP+0xC] (int): Requested maximum frame count (passed on stack)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Success indicator (always returns 1)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2: DT_CelData type identifier\n- 0x4: Offset of cel image pointer in pCelData structure\n- 0x40: Offset of nFrameOffset field in pCelData structure (64 bytes)\n\nNotes:\n- AssertFailure is a fatal error handler (does not return)\n- Validates data type integrity before processing\n- Clamps requested frame count to valid range [0, frameCount-1]",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
