      "name": "CreateObjectByTypeFactory",
      "signature": "int * CreateObjectByTypeFactory(int * pTypeConfig)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int *",
      "comment": "Factory function that creates objects based on type identifier.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract flags from pTypeConfig[7] (NULL-safe)\n2. Switch on pTypeConfig[0] type identifier (1-10, 12)\n3. Call appropriate constructor with parameters from pTypeConfig array\n4. Return created object pointer\n\nParameters:\n- pTypeConfig (int *): Pointer to type configuration array containing type ID and constructor parameters\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to created object (type depends on input type), or NULL if type not recognized\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- Type 1: CreateUIElementType1 (10 parameters)\n- Type 2: CreateUIElementType2 (8 parameters)\n- Type 3: CreateGameObject\n- Type 4-6, 8-10, 12: Various object constructors\n- Type 7: CreateUnit dispatcher\n- Default: Returns NULL\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CreateUIElementType1, CreateUIElementType2, CreateGameObject, CreateUnit\n- Ordinal_10042, Ordinal_10063, Ordinal_10091, Ordinal_10097, Ordinal_10135",
