      "name": "CalculatePopupHoverColumn",
      "signature": "int CalculatePopupHoverColumn(int * pPopupData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Calculates which column the mouse is hovering over in a popup window.\nCalled as a callback from the screen object event system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate object type is 0xB (D2WIN_POPUP)\n2. Check visibility flags via gdwBitMasks_exref (offset +8 AND offset +0)\n3. If not visible/interactive, return 0 (not handled)\n4. Initialize selected column to -1 at offset 0x464\n5. Calculate relative X position from popup bounds\n6. Validate mouse Y is within popup height bounds\n7. Validate mouse X is within popup width bounds\n8. If within bounds, calculate column index: X / 20 pixels\n\nParameters:\n- pPopupData (ECX): Pointer to popup structure (type 0xB)\n  - [0x00] eType: Object type, must be 0xB\n  - [0x08] dwFlags: Visibility/interaction flags\n  - [0x0C] nY: Top Y coordinate\n  - [0x10] nWidth: Popup width\n  - [0x14] nHeight: Popup height\n  - [0x18] nRight: Right X coordinate\n  - [0x464] nSelectedColumn: Output hover column index\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Mouse within popup bounds (column calculated)\n- 0: Mouse outside bounds or popup not visible\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xB: D2WIN_POPUP object type constant\n- 0x14 (20): Column width in pixels\n- 0x119 (281): DWORD index for selected column field (offset 0x464)\n- -1 (0xFFFFFFFF): Invalid/no column selected",
