      "name": "CreateScrollbarObject",
      "signature": "void * CreateScrollbarObject(dword nX, dword nY, dword nWidth, dword nHeight, dword nStyle, dword nIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a scrollbar UI object (0x60 bytes).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 96-byte structure via FogMemAlloc\n2. Zero-initialize all 24 dword fields\n3. Set object type to 5 (scrollbar)\n4. Apply global bit flags from gdwBitMasks_exref\n5. Store position/size params in object fields\n6. Set callback to ProcessScrollbarMousePos\n7. Link to global object list\n\nParameters:\n- nX (ECX): X position, stored at offset 0x0C\n- nY (EDX): Y position, stored at offset 0x10\n- nWidth: Width, stored at offset 0x14\n- nHeight: Height, stored at offset 0x18\n- nStyle: Style flags, stored at offset 0x04\n- nIndex: Index value, stored at offset 0x34\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to initialized scrollbar object\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x60 (96): Object struct size\n- 0x18 (24): Number of dwords to zero\n- 5: Object type ID (scrollbar)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:3c4c759b7761bf14ff36ec0b4c321f80",
