      "name": "ClearTextDataList",
      "signature": "int ClearTextDataList(int * pData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Clears all text data in a linked list by releasing pool allocations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input pointer is non-null and points to type 4 structure\n2. Traverse linked list starting at offset 0x48 (pCurrent = pData[0x48])\n3. For each node in list, release 5 consecutive pool allocations\n4. Follow next pointer at offset 0x1c (pNext = pCurrent[0x1c])\n5. Clear list pointers at offsets 0x48, 0x4c, 0x50, 0x54, 0x58\n\nParameters:\n- pData (int *): Pointer to data structure, must not be null; [0] must equal 4\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success, 0 if input is null or assertion fails",
