      "name": "ConvertAnsiToUnicodeAndSetTextLine",
      "signature": "void ConvertAnsiToUnicodeAndSetTextLine(int * pOutput, char * szInput, int nMaxChars, int nUnknown)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts ANSI/MBCS string to Unicode and forwards to processing function.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 2048-element Unicode array on stack\n2. Initialize each Unicode element with default constructor (1024 times)\n3. Convert input ANSI string to Unicode using win2Unicode\n4. Call FUN_6f9121e0 with converted Unicode string and original parameters\n\nParameters:\n- pOutput (int*): Output pointer (ECX, likely destination for results)\n- szInput (char*): Input ANSI/MBCS string (EDX)\n- nMaxChars (int): Maximum characters (0x400 = 1024, matches Unicode array size)\n- nUnknown (int): Additional parameter for called function\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x400 (1024): Buffer size for Unicode conversion\n- 0x800 (2048): Stack allocation for Unicode array (2 bytes per character)",
