      "name": "SetTextFieldValue",
      "signature": "void SetTextFieldValue(int * pTextData, uint dwValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets a text field value with validation and clamping.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validates that pTextData pointer is not NULL\n2. Verifies that pTextData->dwType == 4 (TextData type)\n3. Clamps nValue to signed 32-bit range [min, 0x7FFFFFFF]\n4. Compares clamped value against maximum (pTextData[0x15] - 1)\n5. Stores minimum of (clamped value, max) to pTextData[0x18]\n\nParameters:\n- pTextData (int *): Pointer to text data structure; offset 0x0 contains type field (must be 4)\n- nValue (uint): Value to set; will be clamped to 0x7FFFFFFF if larger\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x4: Expected type field value for TextData\n- 0x15 (21): Offset to maximum value field in structure\n- 0x18 (24): Offset to value field in structure\n- 0x54 (84): Offset to another size/limit field (read but not directly used)\n- 0x7FFFFFFF: Signed 32-bit maximum value limit\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FogAssert: Called on validation failure\n- FUN_6f91436d: Error handler (non-returning function)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:052a101a230c3ddc22bbf8ff66201a19",
