      "name": "RenderTextBoxContent",
      "signature": "int RenderTextBoxContent(int * pTextBox)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Renders the content of a text box UI control with multi-column and scrolling support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pTextBox is non-NULL and type is 4 (TEXTBOX)\n2. Check visibility flags via gdwBitMasks - return 0 if invisible\n3. Find palette index for background color (0x40, 0x40, 0x40 = dark gray)\n4. If parent handle exists, initialize GFX params and draw background rectangle\n5. Apply CJK font height adjustments for locales 7 (Chinese) and 9 (Korean)\n6. Calculate initial render Y from font height, text area, and margins\n7. Handle horizontal auto-scroll (flag 0x40): adjust scroll offset by text width\n8. Handle vertical auto-scroll (flag 0x80): advance to next line if offset < -lineHeight\n9. Iterate through text line linked list starting at pTextBox[0x14]\n10. For each line, iterate through columns (0 to pTextBox[0x19])\n11. Calculate column X position based on alignment: 0x02=center, 0x10=right-align\n12. Copy column text to buffer, truncate to fit available column width\n13. Render text: selected line uses RenderMultilineUnicodeText, others use standard render\n14. Advance Y by line height + line spacing (pTextBox[0x28] or pTextBox[0x29])\n15. Continue until lines exhausted or remaining height insufficient\n16. Restore default font (1) and return success (1)\n\nParameters:\n- pTextBox (ECX): Pointer to text box UI object (type 4)\n  Offset 0x00: Type (must be 4)\n  Offset 0x04: Parent handle\n  Offset 0x08: Visibility flags\n  Offset 0x0C: X position\n  Offset 0x10: Y position\n  Offset 0x14: Width\n  Offset 0x18: Height\n  Offset 0x40: Padding left\n  Offset 0x44: Padding top\n  Offset 0x50: Text line list head (linked list of text lines)\n  Offset 0x58: Highlighted line index\n  Offset 0x5C: Options flags\n  Offset 0x60: Selected line index\n  Offset 0x64: Column count\n  Offset 0x94: Font index\n  Offset 0x9C: Scroll X offset\n  Offset 0xA0: Line spacing (char)\n  Offset 0xA4: Line spacing (non-char)\n\nOptions Flags (offset 0x5C):\n  0x01: Selectable (enable line selection highlighting)\n  0x02: Center align text\n  0x10: Right align text  \n  0x20: Auto-enabled with 0x01\n  0x40: Horizontal auto-scroll\n  0x80: Vertical auto-scroll\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Text box invisible or invalid\n- 1: Rendered successfully\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Locales 7 and 9 get CJK-specific font height adjustments (6-8 pixels extra)\n- Selected line (flag 0x01) renders with multiline function for highlight\n- Horizontal scroll (flag 0x40) auto-scrolls text wider than box\n- Vertical scroll (flag 0x80) advances visible line when scrolled past top\n\nText Line Structure (at pTextBox[0x14]):\n  Offset 0x00-0x10: Column text pointers (up to 5 columns)\n  Offset 0x14: Color/style value\n  Offset 0x18: Char flag (affects line spacing)\n  Offset 0x1C: Next line pointer (linked list)\n\nDecompiler Notes:\n- extraout_var* are phantom variables from GetCurrentFontProperty() returning byte in AL\n  The decompiler shows undefined3 for upper 24 bits of EAX which are uninitialized",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:acaf0b8b6dcf098e0d1103467d6048ce",
