      "name": "RegisterMessageHandler",
      "signature": "void RegisterMessageHandler(int nContext, dword dwMessageType, int nMessageId, void * pfnHandler)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Registers server message handlers for window messages and events.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate nContext is non-NULL (assert if NULL)\n2. Switch on dwMessageType:\n   - 0: Handle as window message (requires valid window message ID)\n   - 1: Register event handler via SEventRegisterEventHandler\n   - 2: Register JSMS handler via SEventRegisterJsmsHandler\n   - 3: Register ISM handler via SEventRegisterISMHandler\n3. For window messages (type 0), validate message IDs:\n   - Assert fail if WM_COMMAND (0x111), WM_KEYUP (0x100), or WM_KEYDOWN (0x101)\n   - Otherwise register via RegisterServerMessageHandler\n\nParameters:\n- nContext (int): Context pointer for handler registration (non-NULL required)\n- dwMessageType (dword): Message type (0=window, 1=event, 2=jsms, 3=ism)\n- nMessageId (int): Message ID or Windows message constant\n- pfnHandler (void*): Handler callback function pointer\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x100 (256): WM_KEYDOWN - keyboard key down\n- 0x101 (257): WM_KEYUP - keyboard key up\n- 0x111 (273): WM_COMMAND - menu/control command",
