      "name": "RightShift96BitInteger",
      "signature": "void RightShift96BitInteger(uint * pInteger96)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Performs a logical right shift by 1 bit on a 96-bit integer stored as three consecutive 32-bit values.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store the middle uint (pInteger96[1]) in dwCarryBits for carry propagation\n2. Shift middle uint right by 1 and OR with high uint left-shifted 31 bits (pInteger96[1] = (pInteger96[1] >> 1) | (pInteger96[2] << 31))\n3. Shift high uint right by 1 bit (pInteger96[2] >>= 1)\n4. Shift low uint right by 1 and OR with stored carry bits left-shifted 31 bits (pInteger96[0] = (pInteger96[0] >> 1) | (dwCarryBits << 31))\n\nParameters:\npInteger96 - Pointer to array of 3 uint values representing a 96-bit integer in little-endian order\n            [0] = bits 0-31 (low), [1] = bits 32-63 (middle), [2] = bits 64-95 (high)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies the integer in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFunction performs logical shift (zero-fill from left), not arithmetic shift\n96-bit value is treated as unsigned integer\nBit order: [0] contains LSB, [2] contains MSB",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
