      "name": "ScaleExtendedFloatByPowerOfTwo",
      "signature": "void ScaleExtendedFloatByPowerOfTwo(ExtendedFloat * pTarget, uint dwExponent, int nResetOnZero)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Scales an extended floating point number by a power of 2 using precomputed table lookups\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters - return immediately if dwExponent is 0\n2. Handle negative exponents by using negative power table (0x1002ed48) and converting to positive\n3. Reset target mantissa to 0 if nResetOnZero flag is set and dwExponent is non-zero\n4. Process exponent bit-by-bit using divide-by-8 decomposition\n5. For each 3-bit group (0-7), advance to next table section (+0x54 bytes per iteration)\n6. Extract low 3 bits as table index (dwBitPosition & 7) and table offset calculation\n7. Lookup precomputed power-of-2 value from table at (base + index * 12)\n8. Check if table entry requires exponent adjustment (bit 15 set in first word)\n9. If adjustment needed, copy 12-byte entry to stack and decrement exponent field\n10. Multiply target ExtendedFloat by the selected table entry using MultiplyExtendedFloat96\n\nParameters:\npTarget: Pointer to ExtendedFloat structure to be scaled in-place\ndwExponent: Power of 2 exponent value (positive or negative)\nnResetOnZero: Flag to reset mantissa to 0 when scaling begins\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Target ExtendedFloat is modified in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf dwExponent is 0, function returns immediately without modification\nNegative exponents use alternate table starting at 0x1002ed48 (negative powers)\nTable entries with high bit set (> 0x7FFF) require exponent field adjustment\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x1002ebe8: Base address of positive powers of 2 table\n0x1002ed48: Base address of negative powers of 2 table  \n0x54: Byte offset between table sections (84 decimal)\n0xc: Size of each table entry (12 bytes per ExtendedFloat)\n0x7fff: Threshold for exponent adjustment check\n3: Bit shift amount for divide-by-8 decomposition\n7: Bit mask for 3-bit table index extraction\n\nStructure Layout:\nExtendedFloat (12 bytes total):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type   | Description\n0x00   | 2    | wMantissaLow  | ushort | Low word of mantissa\n0x02   | 2    | wMantissaMid  | ushort | Middle word of mantissa  \n0x04   | 2    | wExponent     | ushort | Biased exponent with sign\n0x06   | 2    | wExponentHigh | ushort | High word of exponent\n0x08   | 4    | nMantissaHigh | int    | High dword of mantissa",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
